                        "entry_id": "72e4293d-a753-3dc6-bef5-ddf9a276f939",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A native or resident of the state of Minnesota in the United States of America."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7055919c-a96e-4bfb-abb6-6f834e51613f",
                                "sense_id": "6ab862d7-768b-3704-ab69-cbd1d76a6bc9",
                                "text": "When he was finished, as such, he was wringing wet, and now he had to edge and shimmy his way back, and with a most woebegone look, and everybody laughing, except the sad blond boy, and the Minnesotans roaring in the cab."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a19f2d6-6256-4d58-b3b2-b89538a71d94",
                                "sense_id": "6ab862d7-768b-3704-ab69-cbd1d76a6bc9",
                                "text": "[…] while a Minnesotan in her early thirties summed up the general influence of apocalyptic popular culture: “I think it has made me more of a doomer. […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "356e3268-34be-4f60-932e-f9eca150be48",
                                "sense_id": "6ab862d7-768b-3704-ab69-cbd1d76a6bc9",
                                "text": "\"If you are a true Minnesotan it is gray duck,\" wrote Darold Schaefer. \"If not it would be goose. The only time that gray goose is acceptable is if it is vodka.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
